class:: PV_PitchShiftBella
summary:: Phase-vocoder pitch shifting for FFT chains based on Bela lecture code
categories:: UGens>FFT
related:: Classes/PitchShiftBella, Classes/FFT, Classes/IFFT, Classes/PV_BinShift, Classes/PV_MagShift

description::

PV_PitchShiftBella is a phase-vocoder pitch shifter derived from Andrew McPherson's Bela phase-vocoder course example code::fft-pitchshift::. The Bela Knowledge Base describes the example as converting from phase to frequency, scaling the frequencies, and converting back to phase so pitch changes without changing timing. This version applies the same spectral processing as code::PitchShiftBella:: to an incoming SuperCollider FFT chain.

The algorithm estimates the fractional frequency of the signal in each bin by measuring the phase advance between consecutive analysis frames. It subtracts the expected phase advance for the bin's center frequency, wraps the remaining difference, and uses the elapsed samples between frames to recover the frequency deviation.

During the shifting stage, these frequencies are multiplied by the pitch ratio and their corresponding magnitudes are mapped into the appropriate target bins. When several analysis bins land in the same synthesis bin, their magnitudes are added and their shifted frequencies are magnitude-weighted. The synthesis phase is then reconstructed by accumulating these frequencies over time, preserving phase continuity between successive output frames.

Internally, the UGen keeps separate input and output phase histories and modifies the incoming FFT buffer in place. It returns an FFT chain for further PV processing or code::IFFT::. The analysis transform, windows, and final overlap-add belong to the external code::FFT:: and code::IFFT:: UGens. Frame spacing is measured from incoming FFT updates, so there is no separate hop-size argument to match. The shared algorithm does not imply identical gain or latency to code::PitchShiftBella::, which uses its own buffering and window scaling.

The closest vanilla comparison is code::PV_BinShift::, which also moves spectral content between bins. PV_PitchShiftBella estimates fractional frequencies from phase history and reconstructs synthesis phase; PV_BinShift remaps the complex bin values directly.

classmethods::

method::new

argument::chain
An FFT chain from code::FFT:: or another PV UGen, analyzing an audio-rate source. The FFT buffer must be mono, with a power-of-two size from 256 to 8192 samples. FFT size, hop, and window settings are configured on the incoming code::FFT::. Both complex and polar chains are accepted. The result is a PV chain, ready for other PV UGens or code::IFFT::.

argument::pitchRatio
Pitch ratio. Values are clipped internally to code::0.125..8::; large upward shifts discard bins that move above Nyquist. The value is sampled once per incoming FFT frame. Audio-rate inputs are sampled at the beginning of that server block. Non-finite values use a ratio of 1.

subsection:: Notes

The effect needs successive frames to establish frequency estimates. Allow a short warmup and fade the reconstructed audio in. Hann windows with a hop of 0.125 are a useful starting point. Match the analysis and synthesis window types; overlap and window settings affect the output level. A steady sequence of FFT frames gives the most predictable phase estimates. Freezing, skipping, or heavily modifying phases before this UGen can change the resulting pitch estimates.

Use code::PitchShiftBella.ar:: for the self-contained audio effect. Existing patches that previously used code::PV_PitchShiftBella.ar:: should change that call to code::PitchShiftBella.ar::. The PV version is constructed with code::PV_PitchShiftBella(chain, pitchRatio)::.

